dzn: Skip indirect draws with a draw count of 0

vkCmdDraw*Indirect with drawCount 0, or vkCmdDraw*IndirectCount with
maxDrawCount 0, made Dozen allocate a zero-sized internal buffer. The
allocation failed and vkEndCommandBuffer returned
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY, so the whole command buffer was lost. Such
a draw does nothing, so it returns at once.

From Oliver Bestmann's commit 8f00b5e in github.com/weaselway/mesa (MIT),
where dEQP-VK.draw.renderpass.indirect_draw.* passes (the count_0 case
failed before).

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
index 8b87abe..99fbb22 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -4717,6 +4717,10 @@ dzn_cmd_buffer_indirect_draw(struct dzn_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
                              uint32_t draw_buf_stride,
                              bool indexed)
 {
+   /* Nothing to draw, and a zero-sized exec buffer fails to allocate */
+   if (max_draw_count == 0)
+      return;
+
    struct dzn_device *device = container_of(cmdbuf->vk.base.device, struct dzn_device, vk);
    struct dzn_physical_device *pdev = container_of(device->vk.physical, struct dzn_physical_device, vk);
    struct dzn_graphics_pipeline *pipeline = (struct dzn_graphics_pipeline *)
